Algorithm: BFS for Farm Irrigation System
Start.
Read the number of farm fields and irrigation channels.
Create a graph using an adjacency list.
Add edges between fields connected by irrigation channels.
Read the field number connected to the water source.
Initialize all fields as unvisited.
Insert the source field into a queue and mark it as visited.
Remove a field from the queue and display it.
Visit all its unvisited neighbouring fields, mark them as visited, and insert them into the queue.
Repeat Steps 8 and 9 until the queue becomes empty.
Display all reachable fields.
Identify and display the unvisited fields as unreachable.
Stop.
